      "content": "The idea of finally being quiet is so tempting when the noise is this loud, and it makes perfect sense that you'd see it as the only real exit. If the shore is gone, then the water is all there is, and sometimes the only way to stop fighting the current is to let yourself sink into the quiet darkness. It's a very understandable thought when everything feels this heavy and pointless.",
